  <h3 id="menu-button-fixed-width">
    Fixed Width Menu Button
  </h3>
  <p>
    Use the
    <code>menu-button__menu--fix-width</code>
    or
    <code>fake-menu-button__menu--fix-width</code>
    element modifier to fix the width of any menu items to the button
    width. This is useful in cases where the menu overlay needs to be
    constrained to the button width, usually to accomodate spacing and layout.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>NOTE:</strong>
    Fixed width is currently only available on menu buttons that use a
    <code>span</code>
    root tag.
  </p>

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="demo__inner">
      <span class="menu-button">
        <button
          class="btn btn--secondary"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-haspopup="true"
          type="button">
          <span class="btn__cell">
            <span class="btn__text">
              Button
            </span>
            <svg
              class="icon icon--12"
              height="10"
              width="14"
              aria-hidden="true">
              <icon-symbol name="chevron-down-12"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div class="menu-button__menu menu-button__menu--fix-width">
          <div class="menu-button__items" role="menu">
            <div class="menu-button__item" role="menuitem">
              <span>Menu Item 1 with a long string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="menu-button__item" role="menuitem">
              <span>Menu Item 2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="menu-button__item" role="menuitem">
              <span>Menu Item 3</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <highlight-code type="html">
